+---
+type: spec
+task_slug: ratelimit
+status: approved
+created: 2026-10-15
+tags: [timeparse, spec, python, rate-limiting, token-bucket]
+test_framework: pytest
+interview_rounds: 1
+lane: light
+summary: "Token-bucket RateLimiter (allow / retry_after) in timeparse/ratelimit.py"
+---
+
+# SPEC: ratelimit
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+Callers of `timeparse` need to throttle work to a rate written the same way durations already are (`"5/1m"`). A token bucket gives a steady rate with a bounded burst, and reusing `parse_duration` keeps one duration grammar.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+A caller can build `RateLimiter("10/1s", burst=5)`, ask `allow()` before each action, and ask `retry_after()` how long to wait, with an injectable clock for deterministic tests.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### AC-001: Construction validation
+**Given** a `rate` string, a `burst` and a clock
+**When** `RateLimiter(rate, burst)` is built
+**Then** `"N/DURATION"` with integer N > 0 and a `parse_duration` value > 0, plus an integer `burst` > 0, is accepted
+**And** anything else (missing `/`, non-integer or zero N, zero or invalid duration, `burst` <= 0 or not an int, including bool) raises `ValueError`
+
+### AC-002: Starts full, refills continuously, capped
+**Given** a new limiter with `burst=3` and `rate="1/1s"`
+**When** 3 tokens are taken at t=0, then the clock advances 0.5s, then 100s
+**Then** after 0.5s half a token has accrued (`allow()` is `False`, `retry_after()` is 0.5)
+**And** after 100s only `burst` tokens are available (a fourth consecutive `allow()` is `False`)
+
+### AC-003: allow takes tokens only on success
+**Given** a limiter holding fewer than `n` tokens
+**When** `allow(n)` is called
+**Then** it returns `False` and the token count is unchanged; with enough tokens it returns `True` and deducts exactly `n`
+
+### AC-004: retry_after
+**Given** `rate="1/1s"`, `burst=2`, bucket empty at t=0
+**When** `retry_after(2)` is called
+**Then** it returns `2.0`; it returns `0.0` when `n` tokens are available now
+**And** calling it never changes availability
+
+### AC-005: n bounds
+**Given** any limiter with `burst=B`
+**When** `allow(n)` or `retry_after(n)` is called with `n < 1`, `n > B`, or non-int `n`
+**Then** `ValueError` is raised and no tokens are taken
+
+### AC-006: A token is available exactly when due
+**Given** `rate="10/1s"`, `burst=1`, a fake clock
+**When** `allow()` is called at 0.0, 0.1, 0.2, … 1.0
+**Then** every call returns `True` (despite float error such as `0.3-0.2 != 0.1`)
+**And** `allow()` at 0.05 after the call at 0.0 returns `False`
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- Thread safety / locking.
+- Blocking `acquire`/sleep helpers, async support.
+- Fractional or float `N`, or a rate string without a duration.
+- Handling a clock that goes backwards beyond not adding negative tokens.
+- CLI integration or re-export from `timeparse/__init__.py`.
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | already used in `tests/` |
+| Dependencies | stdlib + `timeparse.parse` only | library has none today |
+| Float tolerance | availability compares with a small epsilon (about 1e-9 tokens) | AC-006: 0.1-step clock readings accumulate float error |
+| Compatibility | Python version of `pyproject.toml` | existing module style (`from __future__ import annotations`) |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| AC-001 | unit | `test_ac001_construction_validation` |
+| AC-002 | unit | `test_ac002_refill_and_cap` |
+| AC-003 | unit | `test_ac003_allow_takes_only_on_success` |
+| AC-004 | unit | `test_ac004_retry_after` |
+| AC-005 | unit | `test_ac005_n_bounds` |
+| AC-006 | unit | `test_ac006_available_exactly_when_due` |
+
+Oracles: AC-001/002/004/005/006 are golden values taken from the task statement (hand-derived). AC-003 and AC-004 also share a property: `retry_after(n) == 0.0` exactly when `allow(n)` would succeed, and after advancing the clock by `retry_after(n)`, `allow(n)` succeeds.
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+none
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Lane `light`: one new file plus tests, one session, no irreversible decision (the API shape is fully dictated by the ask, so nothing is a non-obvious trade-off).
+- Round 1 (auto_full, DRI not asked): float tolerance settled as an epsilon in the availability comparison because AC-006 cannot pass with exact float arithmetic.
+- Defaults: bool is rejected for `burst`/`n`; non-int `n` raises `ValueError`.
+
+## 🔎 Spec Validation
+Advisory, single pass. Assessment: MAJOR_REVISION (descriptive only; nothing gated).
+- **critical** — The public API (constructor signature `RateLimiter(rate, burst, clock=time.monotonic)`, `allow(n=1) -> bool`, `retry_after(n=1) -> float`, `ValueError` contract) is a public API contract but `irreversible_decisions` is `[]`. The signature is fixed verbatim by the task statement; the DRI decides whether to list it.
+- warning — AC-003's "token count" is not observable. Test it through `allow`/`retry_after` only (e.g. full bucket: `allow(n)` then `allow(burst-n+1)` is `False`, `allow(burst-n)` is `True`).
+- warning — AC-001/AC-005 golden tables omit bool, float, negative N, non-numeric N and bad-duration rows that the prose requires. `/hm:execute` Phase A should add them.
+- warning — Clock regression has no AC, and the epsilon is only "about 1e-9". Add a just-before-due case to AC-006 (e.g. t=0.0999 is `False`).
+- suggestion — Golden provenance cites the task statement. Quote it when practical.
